## My recommended architecture

For your background, I would build it like this:

```text
                   React Web App
                         │
                         ▼
                    FastAPI
                         │
            ┌────────────┼────────────┐
            ▼            ▼            ▼
       PostgreSQL       Redis       Celery
            │                         │
            │                         ▼
            │                    Background Jobs
            │
            ▼
       Attendance Engine
            │
     ┌──────┼─────────┐
     ▼      ▼         ▼
    GPS   Geofence   Selfie
     │      │         │
     └──────┼─────────┘
            ▼
        Attendance
            │
     ┌──────┼──────────┐
     ▼      ▼          ▼
   Leave  Payroll    Reports
```

**The key is to build it as a SaaS product from day one** if your goal is to 
eventually rent it to companies. That means multi-tenancy, RBAC, audit logs, 
configurable attendance rules, subscription management, and strong data isolation 
should be part of the architecture rather than added later.


If you only need attendance

I would not immediately pay for a complete HRMS. Look for a service offering:

Employee master
Web check-in/check-out
Mobile attendance
GPS/geofencing
Selfie attendance
Shift management
Leave management
Attendance regularization
Monthly attendance reports
Excel export
Admin/HR login
Employee login
Multiple branches
API access, if you want to integrate it with your own system

For example, Kredily currently has a free plan with web attendance, 
employee self-service and mobile app, while GPS/selfie attendance is 
available on its Professional plan